  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "MsJIKwyWJvXln977kmnRsLaUZ2k=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:40.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "A processor implements `IProcessor` with `onOperations(operations: OperationWithContext[])` and `onDisconnect()`. Each `OperationWithContext` pairs an `Operation` (action type, input, index, hash, timestamp) with `OperationContext` (documentId, documentType, scope, branch, ordinal for cross-document ordering, resultingState as JSON). `ProcessorFilter` has optional arrays: `documentType`, `scope`, `branch`, `documentId`. A field that is `undefined` or `[]` matches everything; a field with values matches when the operation's context value is in the array; all present fields must match. The `\"*\"` wildcard is honored **only in `documentId`** \u2014 in `documentType`, `scope`, and `branch` a literal `\"*\"` matches only an operation whose value is the string `\"*\"`, i.e. nothing real. To match all scopes, omit `scope` or set it to `[]`; never write `scope: [\"*\"]` (the codegen analytics template emits exactly that, and it silently matches no operations). The factory pattern: outer function receives `IProcessorHostModule` (shared resources), inner function receives `driveHeader` per drive, returns `ProcessorRecord[]`. By default processors replay all history; set `startFrom: \"current\"` to skip historical operations.\n\n_Corrected 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:40.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:40.000Z"
    }
  },
